{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QRxiWAmSGPdEuSFHmvk24y","type":"tool_result","content":"1821 PLAN.md\n1:# WIRETAP\n19:## 0. Contents\n42:## 1. The game on one page\n69:## 2. Genre, perspective and why\n79:## 3. Tech stack, architecture and modules\n81:### 3.1 Stack (pin these)\n101:### 3.2 Dev folder layout\n146:### 3.3 Single-file bundle (`tools/build.mjs`)\n160:### 3.4 Architecture rules (non-negotiable; they make attract, bots, network and tests possible)\n170:### 3.5 Scenes\n190:### 3.6 Engine setup (99-start.js)\n206:## 4. Controls and 10-foot UX\n208:### 4.1 Input preset `KEYS` (custom; include moves and the menu keys verbatim, since custom presets don't inherit them)\n224:### 4.2 Context maps (DualSense / keyboard + mouse)\n244:### 4.3 Prompts and glyphs\n255:### 4.4 Gamepad axis inversion (the ~10% inverted-input issue)\n269:### 4.5 10-foot UI rules\n280:### 4.6 HUD (E.Shell `ui.hud` each step; field scenes)\n290:### 4.7 Settings (game group; the engine adds Display/Sound/Comfort/Controls)\n306:### 4.8 Touch-only devices\n315:## 5. Core systems\n317:### 5.0 Shared numbers\n326:### 5.1 Field scene and interactions\n345:### 5.2 Perception: getting \"made\" (08-perception.js)\n376:### 5.3 Watch mode, reading roles and photos (10-camera.js)\n390:### 5.4 Agents and routines (07-agents.js)\n410:### 5.5 Tail (11-tail.js)\n432:### 5.6 Foot chase (12-chase.js)\n443:### 5.7 Stealth search (trash, Ep4) and the long lens (Ep5B)\n447:### 5.8 Raid (13-raid.js, Ep5A)\n460:## 6. Investigation systems\n462:### 6.0 The Annex (hub scene) and the car\n478:### 6.1 The Board (14-board.js)\n492:### 6.2 Notebook (15-notebook.js; Create / Tab)\n501:### 6.3 Pager cipher (16-cipher.js; App. C)\n507:### 6.4 The box: interrogation (17-box.js; App. E)\n525:### 6.5 Paper: affidavit and the judge (18-paper.js; App. F)\n547:### 6.6 The wire room (19-wire.js; App. D) — the signature system\n563:### 6.7 Meters and ops choices (20-meters.js)\n583:## 7. The corner: crew side (09-corner.js)\n585:### 7.1 CornerSim (one system for story, interludes, versus and attract)\n629:### 7.2 Police pressure (for crew-side play, versus and attract)\n634:### 7.3 Playing Tee (interludes)\n647:### 7.4 Interludes (all at night, 5:00 of real time on a fast clock 22:00 → 02:00, CornerSim running; targets are about 70-80% of what the rates allow)\n656:### 7.5 Barks\n667:## 8. Story mode: The Case\n669:### 8.1 Setting\n678:### 8.2 Cast (all original; App. I has voices, §12.4 has colors)\n707:### 8.3 Episode 1: EYES ON (~15 min)\n719:### 8.4 Episode 2: PAPER (~15 min)\n733:### 8.5 Episode 3: UP (~18 min)\n746:### 8.6 Episode 4: DRY CLEANING (~15 min)\n760:### 8.7 Episode 5: THE COUNT (~15-20 min)\n776:### 8.8 Endings and montage\n794:### 8.9 Episode select and saves\n806:## 9. Versus mode and online play: THE GAME (50-versus.js, 51-net.js)\n808:### 9.1 The round\n831:### 9.2 Local play (\"on its own\")\n838:### 9.3 AI Hub: shared-world (AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\n900:## 10. Attract mode (52-attract.js)\n922:## 11. Audio (03-audio.js): all written in code\n924:### 11.1 Music (engine `game.audio.music`, scores in App. H)\n943:### 11.2 Sound effects (`audio.define(name, voice)`; engine voice format)\n968:### 11.3 Ambience beds and voices\n994:## 12. Art direction and world building (05-world.js, 06-people.js)\n996:### 12.1 Mood by time of day (canvas lighting always; GPU lighting where available for night, `game.enableGPU({ map })`, with the same ambient set on both)\n1004:### 12.2 Wall types (App. A legend). Everything gets `cut: true` except low walls.\n1018:### 12.3 Floors (legend values `{ floor: tag }`; `floorTex` per tag, or `floorMats`)\n1033:### 12.4 People and palettes\n1039:### 12.5 Shapes to write (E.SHAPES data, docs/ASSETS.md format; check each with `node engine/tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#id`)\n1060:### 12.6 World details that sell it\n1067:### 12.7 Title screen\n1073:### 12.8 UI look (ui.css and the E.Shell theme)\n1081:## 13. About/Credits screen and the exit interview\n1134:## 14. Build order and milestones\n1156:## 15. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1174:## 16. Testing plan (lightweight and token-efficient)\n1234:## 17. Definition of done (tick every line before shipping)\n1251:# Appendices\n1253:## Appendix A: Penn Row neighborhood map (72 × 56 cells; 1 cell = 16 units; x east, y south)\n1383:## Appendix B: Annex and small interiors\n1411:## Appendix C: Cipher and pages (verified by script)\n1451:## Appendix D: Wire calls\n1495:## Appendix E: Interrogation data\n1534:## Appendix F: Affidavit and the judge\n1555:## Appendix G: Writing guide, key scenes, endings\n1680:## Appendix H: Music scores (engine `audio.music` format; all checked: every bar is 16 steps, notes are valid, the JS parses)\n1737:## Appendix I: Voice profiles (Animalese synth, §11.3)\n1765:## Appendix J: Data schemas and the feature matrix","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a038f438-ab72-4348-9a4c-2f1730dcbd38","uuid":"dc8a36ac-3594-49a8-8cd7-17d0d2f6477d","timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:58:29.140Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1821 PLAN.md\n1:# WIRETAP\n19:## 0. Contents\n42:## 1. The game on one page\n69:## 2. Genre, perspective and why\n79:## 3. Tech stack, architecture and modules\n81:### 3.1 Stack (pin these)\n101:### 3.2 Dev folder layout\n146:### 3.3 Single-file bundle (`tools/build.mjs`)\n160:### 3.4 Architecture rules (non-negotiable; they make attract, bots, network and tests possible)\n170:### 3.5 Scenes\n190:### 3.6 Engine setup (99-start.js)\n206:## 4. Controls and 10-foot UX\n208:### 4.1 Input preset `KEYS` (custom; include moves and the menu keys verbatim, since custom presets don't inherit them)\n224:### 4.2 Context maps (DualSense / keyboard + mouse)\n244:### 4.3 Prompts and glyphs\n255:### 4.4 Gamepad axis inversion (the ~10% inverted-input issue)\n269:### 4.5 10-foot UI rules\n280:### 4.6 HUD (E.Shell `ui.hud` each step; field scenes)\n290:### 4.7 Settings (